      "focus": "Keep practicing hiragana and recognize katakana in loanwords (ノート, ゴム). Japanese nouns usually do not change for plural; quantity and context tell us how many. Use ～つ for general items such as erasers; bound notebooks use ～さつ (にさつ means two notebooks). The object particle を is pronounced o. も means also or too and replaces は or を.",
