    {
      "lesson": 8,
      "moduleId": "foundation-japanese-basics",
      "focus": "Read numbers one to ten. なんにん means how many people; いくつ means how many general items. Use ～さい（歳） for age and an appropriate counter for objects; ～つ counts general items, while ～にん（人） counts people. Some readings change, including ひとり（一人）. に (two) sounds the same as the location particle に; さん (three) sounds the same as the polite name suffix. 18 is じゅうはち, but 18 years old is じゅうはっさい.",
